      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_3",
      "quote": "Worldwide, surgery related deaths within 30 days of the procedure accounts the third contributor among all causes of deaths, with an estimated 4.2 million people annually and half of these deaths occur in low and middle income countries.",
      "reason": "Provides a brief statement of the global burden of surgery-related deaths (context for why surgical outcomes matter) but does not explicitly describe the current state of knowledge or key uncertainties specifically about surgical site infection after cesarean section in Ethiopia or globally; thus only partially meets the requirement."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e2",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_5",
      "quote": "This SRMA included all articles conducted in all regional state of Ethiopia reporting the prevalence/proportion/incidence of SSI after cesarean section and/or associated factors.",
      "reason": "States the review's scope (prevalence and associated factors of SSI after cesarean section in Ethiopia), indicating a need to synthesize evidence for this topic, but does not explicitly articulate the importance or broader rationale (e.g., gaps in evidence, public health impact specific to cesarean SSI) in detail, so the requirement is partially satisfied."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e3",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_10",
      "quote": "Wehave checked the PROSPERO database https://www.crd.york.ac.uk/prospero/displayrecord.php?) to see whether recently published or ongoing projects exist related to the topic to avoid any further unnecessary duplication: This systematic review and meta-analysis were registered in the PROSPERO database with ID no. CRD42023442583.",
      "reason": "Explicitly states that the authors checked PROSPERO for existing or ongoing projects to avoid duplication and that the review was registered, addressing the need to explain relation to similar reviews."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e4",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": "text_5",
      "quote": "This SRMA included all articles conducted in all regional state of Ethiopia reporting the prevalence/proportion/incidence of SSI after cesarean section and/or associated factors. All observational study designs were included in this SRMA.",
      "reason": "The review synthesizes observational studies on prevalence and associated factors rather than interventions; describing an intervention mechanism of action is not applicable."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e5",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": "text_5",
      "quote": "This SRMA included all articles conducted in all regional state of Ethiopia reporting the prevalence/proportion/incidence of SSI after cesarean section and/or associated factors. All observational study designs were included in this SRMA.",
      "reason": "The review does not evaluate complex interventions or delivery contexts (it focuses on observational prevalence and predictors), so a logic model for intervention components and outcomes is not applicable."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "75"
}

